  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) yields a low accuracy of ~48.5%, indicating the RNA-only baseline is weak. The highest-priority uncertainty is which modality carries the strongest discriminative signal. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest direct comparison to config_001: same profile setting (singleprofile), same 'no aggregation/fusion' simplicity, differing only in modality. If image accuracy substantially exceeds RNA, subsequent experiments should prioritize image encoders and multimodal fusion; if it is comparable or lower, we should invest in better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) or multimodal combinations. Resolving this modality question early is critical because it determines the entire direction of the remaining 8 experiments and avoids wasting budget on a modality that is fundamentally weak."
}

